cts\n  completedIssues: 0;\n  teams: [];                        // Always empty for new projects\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. API Endpoint for Project Detail\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/project-detail.ts` (GET handler, lines 4-208)\n\n**Request Format:**\n```typescript\nGET /project-detail?projectId={projectId}\nHeaders: Authorization: Bearer {token}\n```\n\n**Response Format (200 OK):**\n```typescript\n{\n  project: {\n    id: string;\n    name: string;\n    description: string | null;\n    status: string;\n    targetDate: string | null;\n    leadId: string | null;\n    leadName: string | null;\n    leadEmail: string | null;\n    totalIssues: number;\n    completedIssues: number;\n    inProgressIssues: number;\n  };\n  issues: Array<{\n    id: string;\n    title: string;\n    description: string;\n    status: string;\n    priority: string;\n    identifier: string;              // e.g., \"ENG-1\"\n    number: number;\n    dueDate: string | null;\n    createdAt: string;\n    updatedAt: string;\n    teamId: string;\n    teamName: string;\n    assigneeId: string | null;\n    assigneeName: string | null;\n    assigneeEmail: string | null;\n    projectId: string | null;\n    projectName: string | null;\n    cycleId: string | null;\n    parentId: string | null;\n    labels: Array<{ id: string; name: string; color: string }>;\n  }>;\n  milestones: Array<{\n    id: string;\n    name: string;\n    targetDate: string | null;\n    completed: boolean;\n  }>;\n  members: Array<{ id: string; name: string; email: string }>;\n  labels: Array<{ id: string; name: string; color: string }>;\n  activity: Array<{\n    id: string;\n    action: string;\n    createdAt: string;\n    memberId: string;\n    memberName: string | null;\n    memberEmail: string | null;\n  }>;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Additional Project APIs\n\n**Update Project:**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/update-project.ts` (PUT handler, lines 4-194)\n\nSupports updating: `name`, `status`, `description`, `targetDate`, `leadId`\n\n**Delete Project:**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/projects.ts` (DELETE handler, lines 181-200)\n\n**Request Format:**\n```typescript\nDELETE /projects?id={projectId}\nHeaders: Authorization: Bearer {token}\n```\n\n**Listing/Getting Projects:**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/projects.ts` (GET handler, lines 29-113)\n\n**Request Format:**\n```typescript\nGET /projects\nHeaders: Authorization: Bearer {token}\n```\n\n**Response Format includes:** Array of projects with team information, issue counts, and member/team filter options."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a472d8252e0bcf7d9 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 32414\ntool_uses: 6\nduration_ms: 13268</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d79f14e-e24f-460a-9e3f-21530b576549","uuid":"1ce62cc1-9de6-4ac6-9fbf-b775e5592a82","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone, find:\n1. The seed data file (likely in netlify/functions/ or a seed.sql/seed.ts file) - I need to know if there's a project with zero issues in the seed data\n2. The API endpoint for creating projects (netlify/functions/) - I need to know the API for creating a project\n3. The API endpoint for project-detail - to understand the response format\n4. Any existing API for listing/deleting projects\n\nReturn the relevant file contents and paths.","agentId":"a472d8252e0bcf7d9","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found all the files you need. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n### 1. Seed Data File\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n\n**Key Finding - Projects with Zero Issues:**\nThe seed data creates **one project** called \"V2 Launch\" (line 92-96):\n- Name: \"V2 Launch\"\n- Description: \"Version 2.0 product launch with new features\"\n- Status: \"in_progress\"\n- Target Date: \"2026-06-30\"\n- Lead: A